# ============================================================================
#  MILK POP — HTTP security headers  (Block E / WP-03 host contract)
#
#  WHAT THIS IS
#  ------------
#  Vite copies everything in `public/` into `dist/` verbatim, so this file ships
#  as `dist/_headers`. That filename is the response-header convention for
#  **Netlify** and **Cloudflare Pages** — if you deploy to either, these headers
#  apply automatically with no extra config.
#
#  DEPLOYING SOMEWHERE ELSE?  (no host config is committed to this repo)
#  --------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Netlify is the SUPPORTED production host for v1 (netlify.toml is committed;
#  WP-03 decision). This `_headers` file is ignored by hosts that don't read
#  it — if you must deploy elsewhere, docs/HOSTING.md carries copy-paste
#  snippets (Vercel / Nginx / Apache). Whichever host serves the site, the
#  header VALUES below are the single source of truth — keep them identical,
#  and prove the deployed result with scripts/headers-smoke.live.mjs.
#
#  CSP NOTES (read before tightening)
#  ----------------------------------
#   • connect-src allows `https://*.supabase.co` and `wss://*.supabase.co` — the
#     REST API, Storage, Edge Functions and Auth all live under the project
#     subdomain, and the exact URL is a build-time env var not knowable here. If
#     you use a CUSTOM Supabase domain, add it to connect-src.
#   • connect-src also allows Cloudflare Turnstile's verify host is server-side
#     (in the Edge Function), so the browser only needs the Turnstile *widget*
#     script/frame from `challenges.cloudflare.com` when CAPTCHA is enabled.
#   • style-src needs 'unsafe-inline': Vite + Tailwind v4 + the `motion`
#     animation library inject inline styles at runtime, and React writes inline
#     `style` attributes. This is expected for this stack. script-src stays
#     strict ('self') because index.html has no inline scripts — Vite emits
#     external module scripts only.
#   • img-src allows data: (favicon + explicitly supported legacy image data),
#     blob: (local image previews) and `https://*.supabase.co` for the current
#     Supabase Storage media pipeline. All
#     seeded artwork ships from this domain (/brand/…), so no third-party
#     image host is needed or allowed.
# ============================================================================

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://*.supabase.co; media-src 'self' blob: https://*.supabase.co; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://www.youtube.com; manifest-src 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies: none

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ROUTING/SEO: the staff portal and management panel are session-gated app
# screens, not content. robots.txt no longer Disallows these paths (a
# Disallow would stop Google from ever fetching them and SEEING the noindex)
# — these headers plus the runtime <meta name="robots"> are the authoritative
# noindex mechanism. All four path forms are listed explicitly because bare
# `/staff` is NOT covered by `/staff/*` on either host.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CACHING: everything under /assets/ carries a Vite content hash in its
# filename, so a byte change always changes the URL. That makes `immutable`
# correct and safe — browsers may reuse these files for a year without a
# single revalidation request. The app shell deliberately has no custom
# long-lived Cache-Control rule: Netlify's atomic deploy model invalidates old
# deploy objects, while these content-hashed assets remain safe to cache.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Build-generated public fallback and SEO evidence use stable filenames. They
# must follow the active atomic deployment rather than survive as an old
# browser/CDN object after a release switch. The browser also fetches the
# fallback with cache: no-store; these headers make the host contract explicit.
/public-content.json
  Cache-Control: no-store, max-age=0

/seo-manifest.json
  Cache-Control: no-store, max-age=0

# The release marker is the authoritative live-version floor. It must never be
# served from a stale browser or intermediary cache during rollback protection.
/.well-known/milkpop-release.json
  Cache-Control: no-store, max-age=0

/staff
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/staff/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/admin
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/admin/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
